# hash_gate.sh's per-project build-hash manifest (EVENT-MODULARITY-AND-
# BUILD-SPEED.md §2) - derived, machine-local build-cache state, same
# reasoning as the *.+x binaries themselves: regenerated automatically,
# never hand-edited, no reason to track or diff.
.build_hashes.pdl

# Compiled pal-family op binaries (regenerated by each project's own
# build.sh / scripts/build.sh - never hand-edited, no reason to track).
*.+x
system/prisc+x
system/chtpm_parser_pal
system/chtpm_rgb_render
system/keyboard_input
system/renderer
system/gl_mirror
system/egg_window
system/emoji_gen_atlas
system/emoji_xtract

# 2026-10-02 - the same system binaries, but built as native Windows .exe
# (button.ps1 on win32), and nested one or more levels down under a project
# root. The entries above are extension-less and root-relative, so they match
# neither the .exe suffix nor a path like
# x0.../WSR_PAL-PREFERED/system/renderer - all 7 of these were untracked AND
# unignored, i.e. one `git add -A` away from committing build output.
**/system/*.exe

# Generated runtime/session state - grows large, regenerated every launch,
# never meaningful to diff/commit.
pieces/display/frame_history.txt
pieces/display/current_frame.txt
pieces/display/frame_changed.txt
pieces/display/layout_changed.txt
pieces/display/current_layout.txt
pieces/display/active_gui_index.txt
pieces/display/active_gui_is_typing.txt
pieces/display/renderer_pulse.txt
pieces/display/pending_command.txt
pieces/apps/player_app/history.txt
pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt
pieces/apps/player_app/state_changed.txt
pieces/keyboard/history.txt
debug.txt
*.log
rgb_frame.raw
rgb_frame.receipt.txt

# Scratch/backup zips made during this session's own editing work.
y0.claude-temp/*.zip

# REAL SECRET — 2026-08-25, found by a targeted content scan before this
# repo's first-ever commit (going to a PUBLIC repo, github.com/tearitco/
# TEARIT-HQ). A genuine PEM private key, per-user identity keypair from
# the house's own userpal system. Must never enter git history — even a
# later deletion leaves it in prior commits' history on a public repo.
**/user.c54e14cc/priv.c54e14cc.txt

# Frame-dump PNGs + audit receipts (this session's own khtpm receipt-port
# work) - regenerated on-demand, never meaningful to diff/commit.
*-frame.png
*-frame.receipt.pdl
*.png.receipt.txt

# Taskbar/livedesk runtime state (regenerated every launch/session, same
# rationale as the pieces/display/* exclusions above, just under the
# newer #.desktop/ convention this house's khtpm-family apps use).
#.desktop/*_agent_relay.txt
#.desktop/livedesk_launched_pids.txt
#.desktop/*.state.txt
#.desktop/*_action.txt

# Manager-published state files (bookmarks_manager.c / palettes_manager.c,
# 2026-08-25 TPMOS-compliant rebuilds) - regenerated from bookmarks.pdl /
# the emoji pallet / chemistry CSV on every manager tick, never meaningful
# to diff/commit, same rationale as the #.desktop/*.state.txt exclusion
# above (this house's own real "if it's not in a file it's a lie" source
# of truth is the .pdl/CSV, not these published projections).
bookmarks_state.txt
palettes-*_state.txt
.bm_newplus.txt
**/&.widgits/palettes/state/
**/#.#.calendar-dox/BOOK.7z
**/44.xyz.01.00/103.media-studio.7z

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-06 - khtpm/HQ per-app runtime scratch. These are written by a
# running app/manager every launch and every tick; they are never
# "work" and re-appear the moment an app runs. .gitignore stops the
# UNTRACKED ones from cluttering `git status`; the small set that was
# already committed is untracked in the same commit that adds this
# block (files stay on disk, `git rm --cached` only).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
**/module_parent.pid
**/*.pid
**/*_ui.txt
**/*_action.txt
**/*_buffer.txt
**/cli_io_state.txt
**/text_area_*.txt
**/.hq_manager/ui.txt
**/.hq_manager/label.txt
**/music_player_ui.txt
**/music_player_action.txt

# 2026-09-06 - more khtpm/HQ runtime scratch trees (pieces/* under the
# newer @.apps projects, piececraft-hq's per-session state dir).
**/102.agy-txt/pieces/
**/102.editor-*/pieces/
**/@.apps/piececraft-hq/state/

# house backup archives (large binaries — keep only on disk)
x0.parent-level-dev-env-04.04_*.7z

# 2026-09-09 SHARED-SOURCE-COMPILE-IN-PLACE.md — house-authored shared
# .c/.h are compiled in place from &.widgits/_shared-lib/ (via -I), never
# copied into a consumer ops/ dir. Ignore any stray build-copy so it
# can't be re-committed. (Path has an /ops/ segment, so the canonical
# _shared-lib/ copies are unaffected.)
**/ops/khtpm_css_parser.c
**/ops/khtpm_css_parser.h
**/ops/khtpm_render_core.c
**/ops/khtpm_draw_core.c

# proc-lifecycle registry (runtime, PROC-LIFECYCLE-ORCHESTRATOR-TEARDOWN.md)
**/#.desktop/livedesk_proc_list.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-28 - #.desktop/ascii_frames/ (khtpm_core_render.c's terminal-
# mirror frame/receipt/objects snapshots) had grown to ~58,000 tracked
# files. The ledger (index.txt) was already correctly capped at the
# last 50 entries, but the actual <pid>.<seq>.objects.pdl/.receipt.pdl
# snapshot files those dropped ledger lines pointed at were never
# deleted - the cap existed on paper, never enforced on disk (now
# fixed in kh_write_frame_receipt() to unlink both files for every
# entry it trims). This block is the other half: stop tracking this
# directory's contents at all, same rationale as the 2026-09-06 block
# above (regenerated every launch/tick, never "work"). Same convention:
# files stay on disk, `git rm --cached` only, in the same commit that
# adds this block.
**/#.desktop/ascii_frames/
**/#.desktop/strip_ascii_pulse.txt
**/#.desktop/joystick_focused_pid.txt
**/#.desktop/drop_poll.txt

# PRISC-X-FORK-CONSOLIDATION.md — pal VM built from the ONE canonical
# &.widgits/_shared-lib/system/prisc+x.c; no vendored per-project copy.
**/system/prisc+x.c
!**/_shared-lib/system/prisc+x.c
# per-machine window override, do not commit your default_win_w/h - keep it local
*.local.pdl
# hq_ui.local.pdl per-machine window size, see MACHINE-SPECIFIC-WINDOW-SIZING-2026-09-25.md

# ── SECRETS: provider API keys (2026-10-01) ──────────────────────────
# &.widgits/open-hai/state/ was tracked in full, which swept TWO live
# provider keys into git in plaintext:
#   openrouter_api_key.txt
#   tokenrouter_api_key.txt
# AGENTS.md forbids committing keys. They are `git rm --cached`ed below
# (files stay on disk) in the same commit that adds this block, matching
# the house convention already used for the ascii_frames / strip_ascii
# blocks above. NOTE: this only stops FUTURE commits - both keys are
# already in history (first tracked in 5a4164334) and in the origin
# remote, so they need ROTATING, not just untracking.
**/&.widgits/open-hai/state/*_api_key.txt
**/state/*_api_key.txt
**/*_api_key.txt

# Provider keys whose filenames do not follow the *_api_key.txt naming
# convention. raw_poolside.txt is a DIRECT Poolside key (prefix "sky-"),
# which cannot authenticate against OpenRouter - see the Poolside backend
# in ^.hai-horn. Untracked as of 2026-10-01, matched explicitly here so a
# stray `git add -A` cannot publish it.
**/state/raw_poolside.txt
**/raw_poolside.txt
